 "note": "Tienen 'grote omheining' (earthen ramparts, 14th c.) as drawn on the Ferraris map (1777), with its six gates; it stood until 1781. A smaller inner wall (1537-38, 1596) also existed in 1650 and is not traced. Tienen was largely burnt by the French and Dutch in 1635 and rebuilt round the Grote Markt.",
